WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.100
- [Narrator] This is
First Lady Grace Coolidge

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.010
100 years ago on the White House lawn.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.590
She's holding a Girl Scout Cookie.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.200
And this is Tula in 2023.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.350
She's 11 and has been a
Girl Scout for six years.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.670
- I wouldn't say it's well-managed,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.860
but it's so enthusiastically managed

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.340
that you almost end up rooting for them.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.950
- [Narrator] Their success is
due to a number of factors.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.650
Nostalgia, yes, but also
smart sales tactics,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.470
strategic expansions and unlimited supply.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.530
- This year they introduced a new flavor,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.650
the Raspberry Rally,
to be sold only online.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.750
Within hours, it was gone.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.100
There was no stock left.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.013
- [Narrator] This is The
Economics of Girl Scout Cookies.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.310
During the COVID-19
Pandemic, Girl Scouts tried

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.280
to adapt their in-person
tactics to the online world

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.080
with middling success.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.910
- 2021 saw the biggest impact

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.620
in terms of Girl Scout Cookies sales,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.070
because all these troops
were having to balance

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.860
social distancing with
selling their cookies.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.540
- [Narrator] This year,
Girl Scouts have resumed

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.300
in person and booth
sales, but the COVID era

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.000
trend of digital sales
has remained popular.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.440
- I think the girls are mostly unfazed

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.440
because they are quite
nimble with working online.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.250
- [Narrator] Typically,
cookie selling season runs

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.720
from December to mid-April,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.730
but a shortage this year
has forced some regions

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.370
like New York City to sell
cookies later into the year,

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.430
so that the suppliers have
time to bake more cookies.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.140
Even with adapted sales schedules,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.420
Girl Scout Cookie customers
may still be out of luck

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.710
for certain flavors.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.200
This year's new flavor,
The Raspberry Rally,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.420
sold out in hours, but that very

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.660
limited supply could actually
benefit the Girl Scouts.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.760
Because cookies are
typically sold four months

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.593
out of the year,

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:43.770
customers have to get them

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.440
while they're in season or
risk waiting another year.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.600
- The strategy, I think, works really well

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.260
because you keep people's
interest in the cookies

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.760
by introducing new flavors.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.080
- [Narrator] New flavors
can be modeled off

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.400
of best selling ones.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.660
- It just triggers a whole bunch

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.360
of other memories associated
with other Girl Scout Cookies.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.390
You bank on the advantage
that you're giving people

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.960
something new, but that's
also sort of associated

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.700
with something that you're familiar with,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.740
whether it's a cookie
or a childhood memory.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.180
- [Narrator] Certain
cookies that don't sell well

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.460
are phased out, but the
organization makes sure

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.870
to keep longstanding classics,

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.310
like Trefoils and Thin Mints,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:18.810
which have been around in some form

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.850
since at least the 1950s.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.860
- It's a classic marketing strategy.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.890
You can have like say for example,

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.390
a mascara or a lipstick,
that's a classic color,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.060
and something that you
see constant demand for.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.030
To keep a classic like
the Thin Mints around

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.570
is to center the campaign
of selling cookies

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.570
around something that
people instantly recognize.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:43.920
- [Narrator] Girl Scouts list five skills

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.810
troops learn from selling cookies.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.630
Goal setting, decision
making, money management,

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.700
people skills, and business ethics.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.460
- The way that the cookie
program works is that

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.870
you set a goal.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.730
- [Narrator] It helps that
those goals are incentivized.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.220
If you sell enough, you can get prizes.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.670
- I'm trying to sell 2,500
cookies, because if you do that,

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.670
you get a Broadway show as the prize,

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.890
and that sounds really
fun and I love musicals,

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.210
so I definitely wanna go to one.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.070
- [Narrator] Next is decision Making.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.830
A Girl Scout must choose where
and when to sell her cookies,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.320
how to market them and help
decide where her troops

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.060
collective cookies fund should go.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.160
The key player in figuring
out the distribution

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.180
of these cookies...

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.540
- The parent, a lot of the
parents are often troop leaders,

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.270
especially the moms or they participate

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.680
in other parts of the program

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.990
like being a co-cookie chair.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:34.860
They take upon themselves
a lot of the logistics,

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.830
and the planning and where their children

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.950
will be at any given time
to sell these cookies.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.020
- Usually the troop or
a Girl Scouts parents

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.360
purchase the cookies
before any sales are made.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.230
- So they're on the hook
to make up the money

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.460
that they have already spent

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.160
in buying or procuring
the boxes that they said

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.270
that they were gonna sell.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.320
- [Narrator] All sales proceeds,

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.490
according to the Girl Scouts,

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.520
go to the troops to pay for
that year's upcoming activities.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.470
Girl Scouts receive scripts and training

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.060
to get to know the products.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.250
They also receive advice
on their sales pitches.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.890
The goal is to sharpen
their people skills.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.290
- It has definitely helped me talk

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.920
to people and like
communicate what I want.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.720
- [Narrator] Typically,
Girl Scouts sell cookies

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.920
to their family and friends

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.780
or customers in the neighborhood.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.842
- It's still very much
a grassroots movement.

00:04:21.842 --> 00:04:25.890
No one sees it as you know, a big cookie.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.650
No one looks at it as
this big corporate grab

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.173
that you associate with
some of the bigger brands.

00:04:31.173 --> 00:04:34.410
This is as homegrown as it comes.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.610
- [Narrator] Even with the parents behind

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.707
the major operations, the selling point

00:04:37.707 --> 00:04:39.998
is still the Girl Scouts themselves.

00:04:39.998 --> 00:04:42.256
- [Narrator] Don't buy
cookies from an alligator.

00:04:42.256 --> 00:04:44.907
Don't buy cookies from a giraffe.

00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:48.660
Buy cookies from Girl Scouts,
because they're really good.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.810
- There is some criticism
regarding the fact that,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.580
if you're a rich parent,
you can just throw money

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:57.000
at the problem, buy up all
the boxes, you know, done.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.830
The program's done, you've made the money.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.450
Everything's hunky dory.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:01.800
But that defeats the purposes,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.140
many parents have told me,
of teaching their children

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:07.466
financial literacy and having
them go through the process

00:05:07.466 --> 00:05:11.190
of learning procurement,
learning distribution,

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.620
learning sales, and then
learning to manage money.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:14.970
Actual physical money.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.460
You can see them physically,
you know, doing the math

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.560
in their head, calculating
what they've gotta

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.820
give back to our customer.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.360
And I think if a parent
just swoops in and buys

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.790
all the boxes or buys too many boxes,

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.790
it defeats the purpose of
what the program stands for.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.620
- And learning effective sales tactics,

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.500
like offering samples of the
underselling types of cookies

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.390
or encouraging customers to buy more than

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.860
one box of their favorites

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.720
helps the next year run smoothly.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:44.358
- I think the Girl Scout
Cookies inhabit a very unique

00:05:44.358 --> 00:05:48.420
ecosystem when it comes
to selling cookies,

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.020
compared to your everyday brands
that you're familiar with,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.490
whether they're Oreos or any
kind of digestive biscuits

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.440
or whatever cookies that people prefer.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.190
Their main draw is that they are available

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.493
for a very short period
of time every year,

00:06:04.493 --> 00:06:09.120
and you also bank on people's memories

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.227
of eating these cookies
as they were growing up.

00:06:12.227 --> 00:06:13.611
(wrapper rustling)

00:06:13.611 --> 00:06:14.444
- Come out.

00:06:14.444 --> 00:06:17.361
(wrapper rustling)

